		{"id":"b08e253971cc5df7","type":"text","text":"# Smoke\n#### Problem\nSeen as streaklines\n- smoke surfaces\n- different representation - volumetric, particle-based, image-based\n#### Optical model\n![[Pasted image 20250906152220.png]]\n$$\\alpha_{dencity} = \\frac{k}{\\text{area}(\\mathrm{x_0, x_1, x_2})\\cos \\gamma}$$\n$(\\mathrm{x_0, x_1, x_2})$ = triangle / prism\n$h$ = height\n$\\mathrm{p}(t)= e + t r$ viewing ray\n$k$ = slider\n=> denser => more opaque, less dense => less visible\n![[Pasted image 20250906152831.png]]\n","x":-1720,"y":6623,"width":779,"height":1187},
